y contributors via Kaikki / Wiktextract","url":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Geschichte","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24","attribution":"© Wiktionary contributors. Extracted by Wiktextract, distributed by Kaikki.org. Adapted by normalization and selection; shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.","edition":"en","dumpDate":"2026-10-01","extractedAt":"2026-10-21","record":"Geschichte#noun:0"}}],"provenance":{"source":"Wiktionary contributors via Kaikki / Wiktextract","url":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Geschichte","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24","attribution":"© Wiktionary contributors. Extracted by Wiktextract, distributed by Kaikki.org. Adapted by normalization and selection; shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.","edition":"en","dumpDate":"2026-10-01","extractedAt":"2026-10-21","record":"Geschichte#noun:0"},"raw":{"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Geschichte schreiben","bold_text_offsets":[[0,10]],"translation":"to make history","english":"to make history","bold_translation_offsets":[[8,15]],"type":"example"},{"text":"in die Geschichte eingehen","bold_text_offsets":[[7,17]],"translation":"to go down in history","english":"to go down in history","bold_translation_offsets":[[14,21]],"type":"example"},{"text":"Die Geschichte tut nichts, sie ‘besitzt keinen ungeheuren Reichtum’, sie ‘kämpft keine Kampfe’! Es ist vielmehr der Mensch, der wirkliche, lebendige Mensch, der das alles tut, besitzt und kämpft; es ist nicht etwa die ‘Geschichte’, die den Menschen zum Mittel braucht, um ihre - als ob sie eine aparte Person wäre - Zwecke durchzuarbeiten, sondern sie ist nichts als die Tätigkeit des seine Zwecke verfolgenden Menschen.","ref":"1962 [1845], Friedrich Engels, “Hinrichs Nr. II. Die ‘Kritik’ und ‘Feuerbach’. Verdammung der Philosophie”, in Die heilige Familie (Marx-Engels-Werke; 2), page 98; English translation from “Hinrichs No. 2. ‘Criticism’ and ‘Feuerbach’. Condemnation of Philosophy”, in Richard Dixon & Clemens Dutt, transl., The Holy Family (Marx/Engels Collected Works; 4), 1975, page 93:","english":"History does nothing, it ‘possesses no immense wealth’, it ‘wages no battles’. It is man, real, living man who does all that, who possesses and fights; ‘history’ is not, as it were, a person apart, using man as a means to achieve its own aims; history is nothing but the activity of man pursuing his aims.","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[4,14],[219,229]],"translation":"History does nothing, it ‘possesses no immense wealth’, it ‘wages no battles’. It is man, real, living man who does all that, who possesses and fights; ‘history’ is not, as it were, a person apart, using man as a means to achieve its own aims; history is nothing but the activity of man pursuing his aims.","bold_translation_offsets":[[0,7],[153,160],[244,251]]}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","German terms with usage examples","German uncountable nouns"],"links":[["history","history"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Historie"}],"raw_glosses":["(uncountable) history"],"glosses":["history"],"tags":["feminine","uncountable"]},{"examples":[{"text":"eine Geschichte schreiben","bold_text_offsets":[[5,15]],"translation":"to write a story","english":"to write a story","bold_translation_offsets":[[11,16]],"type":"example"},{"text":"jemandem eine Geschichte erzählen","bold_text_offsets":[[14,24]],"translation":"to tell someone a story","english":"to tell someone a story","bold_translation_offsets":[[18,23]],"type":"example"}],"categories":["German countable nouns","German terms with usage examples"],"links":[["story","story"]],"raw_glosses":["(countable) story"],"glosses":["story"],"tags":["countable","feminine"]}],"pos":"noun","head_templates":[{"name":"de-noun","args":{"1":"f","dim":"chen,lein,l,erl"},"expansion":"Geschichte f (genitive Geschichte, plural Geschichten, diminutive Geschichtchen n or Geschichtlein n or Ges